      "message": "The Apple documentation cited at line 250 says:\n\n\u003e Implemented features have a parameter value of 1. Features that aren’t implemented have a parameter value of 0. Non-existent features return an error.\n\nTherefore, the `\u003e 0` check should not be necessary. Is it really necessary to add `\u003e 0`?\n\nUpdate: I see the `\u003e 0` check is apparently intended to handle sme_max_svl_b, which is greater than 1. I probably would add a separate function to get the value of sme_max_svl_b because its value isn\u0027t a boolean.\n\nIf you want to keep it simple and just use this function, please add a comment that if feature is \"hw.optional.arm.sme_max_svl_b\", this function returns whether the value of sme_max_svl_b is nonzero.\n\nI also suggest linking to https://github.com/pytorch/cpuinfo/pull/433 or https://github.com/pytorch/cpuinfo/issues/432 in the comment or in the commit message.",
